                   SINGAPORE CABLEVISION TO TRIAL
         MULTIMEDIA INTERACTIVE SERVICES OVER CABLE NETWORK


      Digital Acts as Systems Integrator; Microsoft to Provide
                          Key Technologies


                 NCTA Digital Booth #4535 West Hall
                NCTA Microsoft Booth #5323 West Hall


LOS ANGELES, Calif., April 29, 1996 -- With support from Digital 
Equipment Corporation and Microsoft Corporation, Singapore 
CableVision (SCV) today announced it has begun a trial of cable 
modem technology using its existing fiber and coax cable network.  
The initial deployment involves high-speed data communications 
capabilities, and is one of the first high-speed data over cable 
efforts in Asia Pacific.  As consultant and systems integrator, 
Digital Equipment Corporation is assisting SCV to prepare its hybrid 
fiber coax (HFC) network to support high-speed, two way data 
communications as well as existing cable TV services.  The initial 
configuration includes Digital's ChannelWorks cable modems and 
Digital's AlphaServer systems.  

     To generate compelling content and media-rich applications, 
Microsoft will provide a suite of Windows NT Server network 
operating system products with the Internet Information Server and 
the Microsoft Internet Explorer browser. The Internet-based content 
will enhance the benefits of multimedia services.  In this trial, 
Microsoft will also provide content from its Internet online 
service, the Microsoft Network (MSN).

     By early next year, the network configuration will evolve to 
include the deployment of third-party cable modems to connect 
approximately 100 households to demonstrate the advantage of the 
high bandwidth cable network.  The cable network was designed 
initially to handle two-way, multimedia transmissions, and this 
trial is the first test of interactive communications.  SCV expects 
the new services will attract local companies to develop 
applications that take advantage of the higher bandwidth.

     SCV has signed a memorandum of understanding with the National 
Computer Board of Singapore to work together on this trial.  It is 
in line with the Board's IT2000 masterplan to make Singapore an 
Intelligent Island with an advanced nationwide information 
infrastructure. Singapore has more than 800,000 homes and about 30 
percent of them have personal computers. SCV has been offering pay 
TV services since 1991.  The construction of the HFC cable network 
started last May.   

     To date, SCV has wired more than 100-thousand households and is 
adding 5,000 households per week.  Singapore is unique in that cable 
drops are installed in every home even if the resident is not a 
customer. Singapore CableVision Pte Ltd is a joint venture involving 
Continental CableVision Inc., Singapore Technologies Pte Ltd, 
Singapore International Media, and Singapore Press Holdings Ltd.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.

     Founded in 1975, Microsoft (NASDAQ "MSFT") is the worldwide 
leader in software for personal computers. The company offers a wide 
range of products and services for business and personal use, each 
designed with the mission of making it easier and more enjoyable for 
people to take advantage of the full power of personal computing 
every day.
