          DIGITAL INTRODUCES A NEW FAMILY OF MULTI-PROTOCOL
  LASER PRINTERS WITH LEADING NETWORK CONNECTIVITY AND FLEXIBILITY


         LN17 Family of Network Laser Printers is Ideal for
                     Heterogeneous Environments


MAYNARD, Mass., April 30, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today reinforced its position as a leading provider of network 
printers with the announcement of the LN17 family of network laser 
printers.  Designed for use in PC, Macintosh and workstation 
computing environments, these 17-page-per-minute network printers 
are an ideal solution for small- to medium-sized, general office 
workgroups in a range of industries including banking, insurance, 
government and legal.

     "By producing printing solutions compatible with virtually all 
operating systems, Digital recognizes users' needs for high quality, 
open printing solutions," said Rob Hannemann, general manager, 
Digital's Printing Systems Business.  "The LN17 and LN17ps printers 
are among the most flexible printers available today -- and are 
another example of Digital's commitment to providing customers with 
low cost, high quality network printing systems."

Superior Networking Capability

     The LN17 family supports Novell IPX/SPX, TCP/IP, Appletalk and 
LAT network operating protocols, which offer versatility to 
workgroups of 10 to 30 users.  The printers also support Adobe 
PostScript Level 2 and PeerlessPrint5E (Peerless System Corp.'s 
PCL5e language emulation) for maximum flexibility and compatibility 
in mixed-platform environments.  The LN17 family also includes 
network printer management software for Novell environments, which 
enables system administrators and end users to easily monitor and 
manage their network printers from a central desktop.

     Additionally, for Windows 95 users, Digital includes 
peer-to-peer printing.  This feature allows users to print directly 
from their desktops on a Windows 95 network, without incurring the 
added cost of a server.  The user also may select a network banner 
page, for easy job identification. The LN17 family also will be 
available in the spring with DECprint Supervisor (DCPS) for OpenVMS 
printing software.

     "Leading network connectivity and flexible paper handling 
options make the LN17 family the most feature-rich printers ever 
developed by Digital," said Bill Streib, president of Prisym 
Technologies, Digital's premiere printer reseller.  "The 
connectivity offered by these printers enables my customers -- the 
end users -- to print high-quality documents quickly in 
mixed-computing environments."

Flexible Paper Handling Options

     The LN17 family offers the most versatile paper handling in its 
product class.  Digital's locking mailbox option ensures document 
security for sensitive, confidential or valuable documents, 
particularly for government or legal offices.  Optionally, this 
device may also be used as a 10-bin collator for managing multiple 
printouts.  The LN17 family is available with optional large input 
and output trays for longer, uninterrupted runtimes, particularly 
useful in shared workgroups.  In addition, these printers, which 
accept a wide variety of standard paper sizes, are available with a 
duplex option to help conserve paper.

High Quality Output

     With standard 1200 by 600 dpi resolution, the LN17 family 
provides high quality output for users in a wide range of industries 
producing word processing, spreadsheets, payroll and database 
management applications. The printers' capability for edge-to-edge 
printing is ideal for offices producing forms and financial 
documents.  An optional hard disk allows storage for fonts and 
forms, and enables job spooling in the printer, which eases print 
queues.  The LN17 family also offers a multilingual front panel with 
selections in English, French, German, Spanish and Italian, an 
attractive feature for multi-national companies.

Pricing and Availability

     The LN17 family includes two models that are available through 
Digital's worldwide network of reseller and distribution partners.  
The affordable LN17 printer, with PCL5e (PeerlessPrint5E) support, 
has a suggested list price of $2,229. For users interested in maximum 
flexibility, the LN17ps printer, priced at $3,099, also includes: 
Adobe PostScript Level 2, additional 4MB memory and a Network Interface.  
The locking mailbox and envelope feeder will be available for both 
models this summer.  For more information within the U.S. call 
800-777-4343, or your authorized Digital representative.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
