      DIGITAL ANNOUNCES WORLD-CLASS BENCHMARK PERFORMANCE RESULTS
         FOR LOTUS NOTES ON DIGITAL'S ALPHASERVER SYSTEMS 

    
MAYNARD, Mass., -- May 30, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corp. 
today announced significant results of benchmark tests to measure 
the performance of Lotus Notes on Digital's AlphaServer systems 
running Microsoft Windows NT. Due in large measure to ease of 
software migration from Intel to Alpha platforms, Lotus has been 
able to ship Notes on Digital's AlphaServer systems several months 
earlier than originally anticipated. This has resulted in making 
the performance results available earlier than planned.

     In benchmark tests conducted by Digital using Lotus 
NotesBench, and audited by KMDS Associates Inc., of Oak Ridge, 
Tenn., Digital's dual-processor NT AlphaServer 2100 5/300 system 
achieved a record-setting 1,625 concurrent users. This represents a 
15 percent improvement over all published and audited Lotus 
NotesBench results for quad-processor Pentium-based servers. Lotus 
NotesBench provides a methodology and tools for measuring Notes 
server performance. 

     "These benchmarks demonstrate that Digital's AlphaServer 
platform provides Lotus Notes users the necessary horsepower to 
address the most demanding application requirements," said Pauline 
Nist, vice president of Digital's AlphaServer Business Segment. 
"Lotus Notes customers are looking for, and can now take full 
advantage of, the industry-leading price/performance, high 
availability, high performance AlphaServer platforms."

     AlphaServer systems provide the capacity to comfortably handle 
the resource-intensive transactions throughout a Lotus Notes 
customer's enterprise. The audited performance test results show 
Notes runs faster on Digital's AlphaServer system than on any other 
competitive offering.

     Digital's plans call for promoting its Alphaserver platform to 
Notes users so that they can take full advantage of these robust 
servers.  The AlphaServer's performance and scalability on the 
high-end provide Lotus Notes customers with the advantage of easily 
consolidating large numbers of servers across an enterprise, 
reducing them to a more manageable number.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organization compete and win in today's global marketplace.
